    "result_text": "That's the complete suite \u2014 Cp01 through Cp11 \u2014 all green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**What the feature does:** When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and another owner already occupies the same household (same last name + address, compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace), the new owner is allowed in and both sides of the join receive the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added a `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically (verified in the generated `OwnerDtoMapperImpl`).\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_id` column. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`AssignHousehold.java`** (new function) \u2014 the pipeline step. When `sharesHousehold` is true and a matching existing household exists, it derives a deterministic, stable id (`H-` + first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over the normalized last name + address), assigns it to the new owner, and back-fills it onto existing household members that lack it. A lone owner (no existing household to join) gets no id \u2014 consistent with the \"shared identifier\" semantics.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHousehold` into the pipeline between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe existing `RejectDuplicateHousehold` step already short-circuited on `sharesHousehold: true`; I left the rejection path intact and added the assignment path after the owner entity is built.\n\n**Tests:** Full suite (21 tests, Cp01\u2013Cp11) passes, including the new `Cp11` household-sharing test and the `Cp10` duplicate-household tests.",
